    "created_at": "2016-12-20T18:59:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-12-20T18:59:06Z",
    "body": "> An important thing to consider in standardization discussions is the concept of the shortest path to interop. If Node simply removes %j, we have achieved interop.\r\n\r\nRemoving features from platforms is pretty painful compared to adding features, unfortunately. :/\r\n\r\nWe can spec out what exists in most common first but I think this discussion is still valuable to be had since we've had it for a **long** time AFAIK.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
