    "created_at": "2017-08-05T22:30:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-05T22:30:02Z",
    "body": "Sure, these are all reasonable points. On the other hand, if one implementation goes out and adds something without a standard in place to support it, it's pretty unlikely that other implementations will follow along, and it's a bad precedent to set. We've done it sometimes (especially in the IE6 days), but in general we prefer a more collaborative working mode.",
